# Ballyrush Banneret: "Kithkin spells and Soldier spells you cast cost {1} less to cast." (CR 601.2f, 118.7a.) Each cast taps exactly
# the reduced cost and the pool is checked right after: empty means the spell took that much and no more. T1 the Banneret itself ({1}{W})
# pays in full (it is not on the battlefield as it is cast). T3 Kithkin Billyrider (a Kithkin, no Soldier, {2}{W}) and Bishop's Soldier
# (a Soldier, {1}{W}) each cost {1} less. T5 Grizzly Bears ({1}{G}, neither) pays in full - the {1} not taken would show as a mana
# left - and Reluctant Dounguard ({2}{W}, a Kithkin Soldier) costs {1} less once, not {2}. Bot2's Dounguard on turn 2 pays in
# full too: the reduction is for spells Bot1 casts.

